# A two-variable UW-CSE-style academic advising model.
#
# Every person has exactly one academic role and one research area.  Advice
# edges are directed from faculty to students, and the soft formulas reward
# matching research areas.  The four unary priors deliberately differ, as they
# would in a learned MLN, so equal cell weights cannot be used to merge areas.

Faculty(X) | Student(X).
~Faculty(X) | ~Student(X).

AI(X) | Systems(X) | Theory(X) | Graphics(X).
~AI(X) | ~Systems(X).
~AI(X) | ~Theory(X).
~AI(X) | ~Graphics(X).
~Systems(X) | ~Theory(X).
~Systems(X) | ~Graphics(X).
~Theory(X) | ~Graphics(X).

~Advises(X,X).
Advises(X,Y) -> Faculty(X).
Advises(X,Y) -> Student(Y).

-0.40 Advises(X,Y)
1.45 Advises(X,Y) & AI(X) -> AI(Y)
1.10 Advises(X,Y) & Systems(X) -> Systems(Y)
0.85 Advises(X,Y) & Theory(X) -> Theory(Y)
0.65 Advises(X,Y) & Graphics(X) -> Graphics(Y)

0.18 Faculty(X)
-0.12 Student(X)
0.16 AI(X)
0.07 Systems(X)
-0.04 Theory(X)
-0.11 Graphics(X)

person = 4
